  "behavior": [
    "Proposal networks use enabled configured network metadata: complete decimal EVM IDs and canonical16-byte Substrate genesis prefixes. Unsupported methods and unrelated ecosystems are excluded. Optional namespaces permit supported Substrate-only wallets without hard-coded DOT/SORA/Ethereum requirements.",
    "Import requires the exact current acknowledged/unexpired approved session with peer and namespace continuity. Base and chain-scoped grants resolve CAIP accounts and methods through the shared session validator; proposal fields cannot supply missing accounts.",
    "The existing mobile account model stores exactly one32-byte Substrate identity and at most one approved EIP-155 identity. SS58 aliases collapse to decoded identity; multiple roots/EVM identities and EVM-only sessions reject.20-byte Polkadot accounts never fabricate an EIP-155 mapping.",
    "Each window owns its caller-generated attempt ID and one subscription. The single approval observer survives cancellation during provider initialization/connect/QR display and retires a late new session. A foreign port cannot subscribe/cancel; rejected attempts cannot disconnect previously known or already imported sessions.",
    "Closing/unmounting cancels the background attempt and releases the window callback. Repeated results cannot replace an earlier terminal state, early results wait for subscription acknowledgement before cleanup, and transport failures return translated failure feedback.",
    "New pairing cannot switch an account after the user changes wallets; duplicates include decoded Substrate identity and already mapped EVM identity. Available networks are derived from current approved matching accounts.",
    "The obsolete method logging complete WalletConnect URIs is removed. Completion rows use a scoped responsive grid and scrolling container to keep all social links and Continue reachable on compact windows."
  ],
